 and I've confirmed that the SmolVLA M=32 prediction range of 58-65% already aligns with the existing measured mean of 60.1±1.3, so that's already validated. Now I need to finalize the YAML structure and determine which tables and figures will best present these findings.\n\nI'm noticing the unified pruning protocol plan lists only one experiment ID but the description covers multiple k values across different states—some running, some planned—so I'll need to map those carefully. The L2 norm results actually support the hypothesis about uniform information distribution in the MLP projector, which is a clean narrative. I should also incorporate the OpenVLA random pruning seed replications that are currently running but not yet assigned to a plan, linking them back to the relevant protocol.\n\nFor the figures, I need a pruning curve comparing L2-norm against random baselines on OpenVLA, a VTR M-curve similar to what exists for SmolVLA, and an updated taxonomy table that accounts for all the seed replications.\n\nLet me verify the exact status of those k values—the description mentions k=0.9/0.95 queued and k=0.7/0.5/0.3 in various running states across specific job IDs.\n\nSince all five k-values are actually being tested, I should include the complete set in the YAML: the three OpenVLA VTC-only configurations with different M values, all five L2-norm pruning experiments across the k-values, the X-VLA seed replications, and the OpenVLA random seed replications.\n\nWriting the final YAML configuration...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7907,"cache_read_input_tokens":45722,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7907},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3d809dbe-96aa-4b7a-8b95-05649ec7187f","uuid":"bfbe1e2b-7f